# BidlowAI non-negotiable #5.
#
# Without this, the same file checked out on Windows (CRLF) and Linux/CI (LF)
# looks modified in git even though nobody touched it. That false drift has
# already cost real time across the estate — it makes review noise, hides real
# changes, and produces "hundreds of changed files" diffs on a clean checkout.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what is text, stores it with LF in the
# repository, and checks it out as LF. One canonical form everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfiles are generated. Keep them LF and out of diff review.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated

# Binary assets — never line-ending converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they will not execute on Linux/CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
